   "text": "I read the molecule in three parts and joined them with an E-alkene\u2013CH2\u2013amide linker.\n\n- **Left part:** a 2,2-diphenyl-1,3-benzodioxole. It carries a trifluoroacetyl group (C(=O)CF3) at position 5 and the amide carbonyl at position 7. The amide carbonyl sits on the ring carbon next to the carbon bearing the lower dioxole oxygen.\n- **Linker:** the amide N\u2013H connects to CH2 (7\u2032), then an E-configured CH=CH (6\u2032, 5\u2032), which attaches to C4\u2032 of the sugar.\n- **Right part:** a 2\u2032,3\u2032-O-isopropylidene ribofuranose bearing adenine through N9 at C1\u2032. The thick bonds at the bottom of the furanose show the usual D-ribo arrangement. I took the stereo tags from the known 2\u2032,3\u2032-O-isopropylideneadenosine SMILES (recalled, not derived from the drawing) and replaced the 5\u2032-CH2OH with the vinyl linker, which keeps the neighbour order and so the same tags.\n\nI checked ring-closure numbers for reuse and balanced parentheses by hand.\n\nSMILES: CC1(C)O[C@@H]2[C@H](O1)[C@@H](/C=C/CNC(=O)c1cc(C(=O)C(F)(F)F)cc3OC(c4ccccc4)(c4ccccc4)Oc13)O[C@H]2n1cnc2c(N)ncnc12"
